WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.787
OT security monitoring provides visibility into industrial assets, communication, access,

00:00:04.787 --> 00:00:07.130
engineering activity, and operational change.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:12.755
Its purpose is to detect and explain security-relevant conditions while respecting safety,

00:00:12.755 --> 00:00:15.098
reliability, availability, and process constraints.

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:19.785
Useful telemetry comes from network traffic, controllers, HMIs, engineering workstations,

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:23.535
historians, remote-access systems, firewalls, endpoints, and identity platforms.

00:00:23.535 --> 00:00:30.565
Passive collection is often preferred around sensitive systems because it observes without actively probing them.

00:00:30.565 --> 00:00:33.846
Protocol awareness adds meaning to industrial communications.

00:00:33.846 --> 00:00:38.064
Baselines define expected assets, peers, protocols, timing, and roles.

00:00:38.064 --> 00:00:39.470
Anomalies identify change,

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:45.094
but operator and engineering context determines whether that change is approved maintenance,

00:00:45.094 --> 00:00:48.844
a process fault, control failure, or cyber activity.

00:00:48.844 --> 00:00:53.531
Good alerts support investigation with asset identity, evidence, process context,

00:00:53.531 --> 00:00:54.937
and safe escalation.

00:00:54.937 --> 00:00:59.155
Monitoring assists incident response by providing timelines, affected systems,

00:00:59.155 --> 00:01:01.499
communication paths, and activity records.

00:01:01.499 --> 00:01:05.717
Findings should update inventory, vulnerability priorities, detection, and architecture.

00:01:05.717 --> 00:01:11.810
Integration with the SOC creates consistent workflows while preserving OT expertise and authority.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:16.497
The strongest programs combine reliable telemetry, documented coverage, tuned detection,

00:01:16.497 --> 00:01:20.715
practiced response, and collaboration among security, operations, and engineering.

00:01:20.715 --> 00:01:24.464
Monitoring cannot guarantee that incidents will not occur,

00:01:24.464 --> 00:01:29.620
but it can replace dangerous uncertainty with evidence and coordinated action.
